          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">March to May: Prime Tiger Sightings</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Tall elephant grass has withered or been cut, unlocking open visibility across the understory. As temperatures climb to 32–38°C (90–100°F) and water sources dry up, tigers spend extended hours at permanent river pools. Best for big cat photographers.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 text-xs text-amber-800 font-bold">
            Tiger Sighting Rate: 75% to 85%
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Season 2: October to November -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 shadow-sm hover:shadow-lg transition-all">
          <div class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-[11px] font-bold bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 border border-emerald-200 uppercase tracking-wider">
            Ideal Climate & Lush Forests
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">October to November: Crystal Skies</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Monsoon rains have washed the atmosphere clean. Forests are vibrant emerald green, rivers are full, and temperatures are pleasant (24–28°C / 75–82°F). The premier season to pair a Terai safari with cultural stays or Himalayan foothill trekking.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 text-xs text-[#0e8354] font-bold">
            Tiger Sighting Rate: 55% to 65%
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Season 3: December to February -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 shadow-sm hover:shadow-lg transition-all">
          <div class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-[11px] font-bold bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 border border-slate-200 uppercase tracking-wider">
            Mists & Migratory Birds
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">December to February: Atmospheric Winter</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
